  "starterCode": "def pandas_resetting_index(df_data: list, index_col: str, drop: bool = False) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Resetting Index** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\ndef pandas_resetting_index(df_data: list, index_col: str, drop: bool = False) -> list:\n    res = []\n    for r in df_data:\n        d = dict(r)\n        if drop and index_col in d: del d[index_col]\n        res.append(d)\n    return res\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
